<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Caterpillar to get tough on strikers.</title>
<headline>Belgian Caterpillar to get tough on strikers.</headline>
<dateline>GOSSELIES, Belgium 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian unit of U.S. moving equipment maker Caterpillar said it might start sacking workers if they reject management proposals to end a long-running strike.</p>
<p>Company spokesman Marc Simonart said investment in the plant could also be halted and parts of the operation might be moved to other locations.</p>
<p>Workers are being ballotted on Wednesday on management efficiency proposals which include voluntary early retirement and aim to achieve 1.8 billion francs of economies over five years.</p>
<p>Staff have been on strike for over 40 days. Three attempts at arbitration have failed.</p>
<p>The plant currently employs some 3,500 workers.</p>
